      "reasons": [
        "The packet describes anticipatory guidance as targeting “early protective feeding practices” in an intervention for parents (child age 6 to 12 months), but it does not support the broader claim that anticipatory guidance is advice “to help parents prepare for upcoming child-care practices.”",
        "While the packet supports content related to feeding and mealtime routines/habits (e.g., increased vegetable/fruit intake and “more beneficial mealtime routines”), the definition’s framing about “upcoming child-care practices” is not explicitly supported by the provided text."
